   .. group-tab:: RTC

      .. admonition:: Defective SPI bitbang driver in Zephyr
         :class: danger

         Access to the RTC module in half-duplex operation mode is not (yet)
         possible. The bitbang SPI controller driver does not (yet) support
         bulk transfers, which is the simultaneous writing and reading within
         a single SPI transfer context, in half-duplex mode with a given dual
         Tx/Rx buffer. The RTC driver requires this functionality. This can be
         identified by the following error message at boot time:

         .. container:: highlight highlight-console notranslate no-copybutton

            .. parsed-literal::

               [00:00:00.001,000] :rd:`<err> spi_bitbang: Both RX and TX specified in half duplex mode`

      .. container:: highlight highlight-console notranslate

         .. parsed-literal::

            :bgn:`uart:~$` **rtc get rtc_extern**
            :brd:`device rtc_extern not ready`

      .. container:: highlight highlight-console notranslate

         .. parsed-literal::

            :bgn:`uart:~$` **rtc set rtc_extern 2013-12-11T10:09:08**
            :brd:`device rtc_extern not ready`
            :bgn:`uart:~$` **rtc get rtc_extern**
            :brd:`device rtc_extern not ready`

         .. .. parsed-literal::

            :bgn:`uart:~$` **rtc set rtc_extern 2013-12-11T10:09:08**
            :bgn:`uart:~$` **rtc get rtc_extern**
            2013-12-11T10:09:16.000
